WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.830
From a low-budget show on TruTV to a globe-circling
phenomenon, Impractical Jokers is this century's

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.220
little comedy show that could.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.920
Compulsively watchable and impossible to watch
at the same time, the good-natured cringe

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:18.870
comedy stars lifelong pals Joe Gatto, James
"Murr" Murray, Brian "Q" Quinn, and Sal Vulcano,

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.880
who grew up performing comedy together in
Staten Island, New York.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.900
Together, the four produce and act out some
of the best grown male buffoonery you can

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.340
find on television today.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:33.800
"I run a project where I bring pictures of
girls in bikinis to prisoners in exchange

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.020
for woodworkings."

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.500
From their original intentions for the show
to the most angry mark they ever pranked,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.620
here's the facts you didn't know about Impractical
Jokers.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.400
"Let the ceremony begin!"

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.420
Jokers: The Next Generation

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.380
You know what Impractical Jokers doesn't have?

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.240
A really prim and proper narrator.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.239
But in their original pitch, they wanted one,
and had the perfect guy in mind.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:08.591
"When we first created the show, we wanted
the narrator to be Patrick Stewart, and we

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.060
wanted him to hate us."

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.660
"Ha."

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:21.620
As fans are aware, it didn't work out but
it was a pretty inspired idea.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:27.060
In the Jokers' minds, Stewart would spend
the episodes hating the show, openly disparaging

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.280
the Jokers as they went about their pranks.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.400
"He would introduce every challenge and he'd
be like these d---- are at it again".

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.420
To Stewart's credit, he's already had more
than enough of a guy named Q.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.620
Murr's cringeworthy debut

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.380
On paper, James "Murr" Murray is the most
professionally put-together of the Impractical

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:49.780
Jokers, with his position as a seasoned producer
and an ample amount of showbiz savvy.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.630
Of course, even talented people have to work
up to their biggest successes and what comes

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.539
before the success can be really rough.

00:01:57.539 --> 00:02:02.609
Murr got a harsh reminder of his indie film
roots with a challenge involving his disastrous

00:02:02.609 --> 00:02:07.840
first feature film, Damned!, which he wrote,
produced, and directed in 1998.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:13.460
As part of a punishment in the episode "Damned
If You Do," Murr was forced to watch a packed

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:17.952
screening of his first movie, suffering through
an embarrassing Q&amp;A session in front of the

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.580
audience after it wrapped up.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.620
"Possibly the budget was very tight."

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.860
The budget was about $25,000 to $30,000."

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:35.460
Following the misadventures of a modern-day
teenage Jesus, Murr's expensive debut is embarrassing.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.640
The most incredible thing about the movie
is that it cost $30,000 to make.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.440
From the look of the finished product, it's
like only fifty dollars ended up onscreen.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:49.240
"Orson Welles was in his 20s when he made
Citizen Kane, what's your excuse?"

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:57.200
After the episode, TruTV uploaded the entire
52-minute movie to its website for free streaming,

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.310
kicked off with a new intro from Murr.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:04.470
So if you want to see the story of the Bible,
but with a lot more butt rock on the soundtrack,

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.620
you, and only you, should definitely check
it out.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.840
Shut down at the ball game

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:15.090
Much of Impractical Jokers' tension lies in
peoples' reactions to the pranks, and waiting

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.040
to see whether they're going to play along
or throw a punch.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.600
"Who threw the chicken at me?

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.480
I want the guy right now."

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.960
"Ah I'll be on the  lookout."

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:30.980
Turns out, seeing someone absolutely lose
it on the Jokers is actually extremely uncomfortable.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:35.460
According to Joe, the angriest person the
production ever encountered took place at

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.680
Citi Field.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:41.650
The prank, a punishment for Joe, involved
stealing baseballs autographed by Mets pitcher

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:46.220
Noah Syndergaard from the funniest possible
victims little kids.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:51.960
The sight of Joe casually robbing young baseball
fans of their souvenirs is one of those atrocious

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:57.010
ideas that the series is so good at but things
went off the rails when one mark went full

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.140
mama bear on him.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.700
"You cannot do that!

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.500
Give me the ball!

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:02.200
That's wrong!

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:03.460
This one?"

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:08.840
According to Joe and executive producer Pete
McPartland, the mother was so furious that

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.560
the whole production was derailed.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:17.600
"No, Never, ever, in a million years has anyone
been that upset at anyone on Impractical Jokers."

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:19.440
That is… until this happened.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:20.960
"Do you think this is funny?

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.460
Do you think this is f------ funny?

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:25.520
No, see what it is ...come here!"

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:33.840
Even after the situation was explained, the
anonymous, giant gentleman waited outside

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.410
for Murr to appear so he could finish the
job, and wouldn't allow his face to be on

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:38.910
television.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.000
Sexist or racist?

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:47.240
Cringe comedy is baked into Impractical Jokers'
DNA, but it can still make the show torture

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.000
to watch.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.940
The Jokers never look worse than the times
they're forced to personally antagonize people

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.810
based on their gender or race.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.580
"The Michelle Obama thing… she got there
because she ah ah ah… slept with a man."

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:04.960
In one "Ask the Jokers" aftershow, Joe was
asked by a viewer whether it's more difficult

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.040
to pretend to be sexist or racist.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.480
"I'm trying to think of the right answer here,
because either way feels like a trap."

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:17.160
After a couple minutes of thinking about it,
Joe came to the conclusion,

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.620
"It's probably harder to pretend to be sexist."

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.920
It's not too surprising of an answer.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:25.060
These jokers are Italian boys from Staten
Island, after all.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.380
Of course they defend the honor of their mothers
and sisters first.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:29.560
"Hello?"

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:30.920
"Hey Ma, what are you doing?"

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:32.860
"I'm at work."

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.000
"I hate you you bitch!"

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:37.600
Background focus

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.900
One accusation that's dogged Impractical Jokers
over the years is the same one that gets lobbed

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.480
at every reality show: "This is fake."

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:51.480
For the most part, these accusations are off-base
but sometimes viewers can raise real questions,

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:56.220
especially when they spot the same extras
participating in completely different episodes.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.940
Fortunately, you don't have to be too skeptical
about the show.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.760
Q addressed the issue head-on in 2018, saying,

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.180
"We don't use actors.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:08.660
We use the people who go to focus groups a
lot and sometimes the same person shows up.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.210
But they never realize they are on the show
for some reason."

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:13.620
"Can I tell you where I think I know you from?"

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:14.120
"Yeah."

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.120
"But not right now.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.220
Because where you think you know me from is
happening."

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:18.000
"Oh"

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:20.940
The last resort

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:26.160
Impractical Jokers' sole mission is to be
weird in public and get the funniest footage

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:26.660
possible.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:31.500
Once the production gets that footage, they'll
go to just about any length to make sure they

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.040
can use it.

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:37.200
In order to show interactions in their unobscured
glory, the production has to get signed releases

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:41.520
from every mark they want to use onscreen
which can be pretty tricky after they've spent

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.740
five straight minutes making someone angry
on purpose.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:48.450
Asked on Reddit if the production ever hands
out money to people that they're pranking,

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:49.080
Sal said,

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.440
"Usually people are pretty cool when they
find out it's a show.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:57.820
The few who get mad we try to convince otherwise,
or they get blurred, or cut from the show.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:02.320
On rare occasion[s] if the person was gold,
we try and throw them a few bucks to coerce

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:02.880
them."

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.020
Our advice?

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.960
Keep that info in the back of your mind, just
in case the Jokers ever happen to pull a prank

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:08.460
on you.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:14.020
No matter how you really feel about it, your
best move is to get mad, stay mad and get

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:14.580
paid.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:19.540
"ah."

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:23.100
Thanks for watching!

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.800
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.340
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

